// # Fleet Dashboard v2 — Per-Repo Health + Trend Sparklines (Proposal)
//
// Logline: Extend status.openooda.org with a fleet-health board fed
//          by fleettick's own state file and alert spool — zero
//          changes to the tick itself.
//
// Setup:   Data contract verified against sweep_main.oo on
//          wip/ringmaster-ringmaster-wC: every tick packs all verdict
//          lines into /Projects/openOODA/.fleet-state.txt and spools
//          ALERT files into /Projects/openOODA/.fleet-alerts/.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Source contract (what the state file already gives us).
//   2. New surfaces (page, JSON, history, refresh driver).
//   3. Verdict -> severity map for chips and sparklines.
//   4. Refresh cadence options with recommendation.
//   5. Risks and honest limits.

## 1. Source contract (read-only, no fleettick changes)

`.fleet-state.txt` — rewritten every 600s tick, fixed section order:

| Section | Line shape | Example |
|---|---|---|
| repos | per-repo dirty state | `openOODA DIRTY=WIP`, `<repo> CLEAN` |
| quota | ledger + pane meters | `QUOTA <agent> <n>`, `QUOTA panes UNREADABLE` |
| workspaces | herdr agent inventory | `AGENTS <n> ...` |
| health | host gauges | `HEALTH load=<x>`, `HEALTH mem use=<n>` |
| forge | github ls-remote probe | `FORGE SYNC` / `FORGE ERR` |
| reconcile | per-repo verdict | `RECON <repo> SYNC|AHEAD|BEHIND|DIVERGED|PULLED|PULL_ERR|DIRTY-SKIP|NO-TRACK|DETACHED|FETCH_ERR|GATE-SKIP|ERR` |
| snapshot/alerts | write + spool receipts | `SNAP <path> lines=<n>`, `ALERT*`, `ALERT_CLEAR` |

`.fleet-alerts/` — one file per live breach, removed on recovery.
This is the breach truth: spool dir non-empty = something is red.

## 2. New surfaces (website repo, zero-build static)

- `src/fleet_refresh.oo` — refresh driver (dogfood law): reads the
  state file + spool dir via &FsReadCap, writes `status/fleet.json`
  and appends `status/fleet_history.jsonl` via &FsWriteCap. No
  ProcessCap — pure file work; the state file IS the subprocess
  product already.
- `status/fleet.json` — current tick digest: sections, per-repo
  verdicts, health gauges, live alerts, tick timestamp.
- `status/fleet_history.jsonl` — append-only, tick-grain dedupe
  (same tick -> replace line), rolling 7-day window (~1000 lines).
- `status/fleet.html` + `js/fleet.js` — board page, terminal-house
  style, linked from index footer as [FLEET HEALTH].

## 3. Verdict -> severity map (chips + sparklines)

| Severity | Verdicts | Chip |
|---|---|---|
| 0 ok | SYNC, CLEAN, PULLED | green |
| 1 note | AHEAD, BEHIND | cyan |
| 2 warn | DIRTY-SKIP, DIRTY=WIP, NO-TRACK, DETACHED, GATE-SKIP, QUOTA warn | amber |
| 3 bad | DIVERGED, PULL_ERR, FETCH_ERR, FORGE_ERR, ERR, QUOTA cutoff, ALERT spooled | red |

Sparkline per repo: last ~24 ticks (~4h at 10-min grain) as
severity-colored cells, newest right. A green strip that flashes
amber then red IS the flap signature; stable-warn repos show as
steady amber. ALERT history overlays the spool open/close times.

## 4. Refresh cadence — the real design tension

quota.json ships via commit+push — fine daily, wrong for 10-min
fleet data (144 commits/day of git-log noise).

| Option | Mechanism | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| A. timer+push | fleetdash.timer runs refresh, commits, pushes every tick | REJECT — history spam |
| B. refresh writes to a served dir | driver writes JSON under the status host's docroot directly; page fetches it | RECOMMENDED — status host is fleet-side; git only sees the code |
| C. hourly commit | refresh runs per-tick to a staging dir; a slower job commits a compacted digest | fallback if B unavailable |

Page remains static; only the JSON transport differs from quota v1.

## 5. Risks and honest limits

- Fleettick is not live yet — state file is soak-era until cutover
  flips; board ships with a visible "state as of <ts>, tick cadence
  600s" stamp and renders whatever the file holds.
- Per-tick flap fidelity requires option B's cadence; committed
  history is always lagging — acceptable, the alert spool is the
  authoritative breach signal anyway.
- RECON only covers repos under the fleet root; the wider 383-repo
  fleet is out of scope for v2 (a fleet-392 sweep is its own lane).
- Page Rule: fleet_refresh.oo stays under 256/8/40; quota_refresh
  pattern (qsrc + driver split) is the template.
